        "original_id": "7eb6548d-9c17-5c13-9c27-3f8362a48771",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Howard, William Small\n- Organizations: Baltimore and Ohio Railroad\n- Places: Maryland, Baltimore, Sandy Hook\n- Buildings: McKim's School\n- Roles: American mechanical engineer, architects\n\nFacts:\n- William Howard was born in 1793 and died in 1834.\n- William Howard was an American mechanical engineer.\n- William Howard was one of the first people to work for the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad.\n- At first, the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad was located entirely in Maryland.\n- The original line of the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad ran from the port of Baltimore west to Sandy Hook.\n- McKim's School was designed by Baltimore architects William Howard and William Small.\n- McKim's School was erected in 1833.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
